{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A bare CI error log tells you where the test gave up, not what the page actually looked like — turn on Playwright's trace so the next flaky failure comes with a real timeline instead of a guess.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Use <code>trace: 'on-first-retry'</code> (needs retries enabled) or <code>'retain-on-failure'</code> so failed tests save a full DOM/network/console timeline as a CI artifact, at effectively no cost to passing runs.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">The DOM snapshots are what close the debugging gap a video can't — they let you find the actual overlay/timing/race root cause, not just watch pixels. Budget for trace storage and upload them as linked CI artifacts, or the capability is invisible when it matters most.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
